@@ -26,6 +26,34 @@ After installing a candidate HWC, independently verify on a background Android
 startup that KWin reports no mapped `Waydroid` window, while a normal app launch
 still produces its application window with the expected size and scale.
 
+## Input FIFO lifecycle
+
+`input-fifo-lifecycle.c` calls the same `input-fifo.h` helper as the native HWC
+input bridge. It verifies replacement of a stale non-FIFO node, ownership and
+permissions, idempotent setup, and detection of a replaced FIFO inode while the
+producer still holds the old descriptor.
+Build and run it without an Android or Wayland session:
+
+```sh
+cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
+  hwcomposer/tests/input-fifo-lifecycle.c \
+  -o /tmp/waydroid-input-fifo-lifecycle
+/tmp/waydroid-input-fifo-lifecycle
+```
+
+The HWC creates the pointer, touch, keyboard, and tablet FIFOs before the first
+Wayland registry roundtrip. This lets Android EventHub discover them during its
+initial scan. The producer checks the FIFO inode before each event and reconnects
+after a container-side replacement; no polling service or shell launcher is
+needed.
+
+`waydroid-input.rc` prepares `/dev/input` as `system:system` mode `0770`
+during Android init, before the composer service starts. The composer runs as
+the host UID with primary group `system`; its FIFOs are owned by its actual
+UID and group, mode `0660`. InputReader accesses them through group `system`.
+The bridge does not attempt privileged chown or create a world-writable input
+directory. The runtime package installs this init action alongside the module.
+
 ## Baikal incremental build
 
 The native build cache is `~/.cache/waydroid-native-build/build/`. The
